    {
      "chord_quality": "sus4",
      "function_role": "avoid-note-free-practice-context",
      "narrative": "Bergonzi prescribes playing modal scale sequences over a dominant sus4 chord specifically to remove avoid-note constraints, allowing the player to hear the pure sound of the key without harmonic interference. 'In the example below all of the notes are played over a dominant sus 4 chord. This allows you to hear the sound of the key without having to deal with any avoid notes.' Chapter 28, p. 113.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "jerry-bergonzi:melodic-rhythms-vol-4:polyrhythmic-construction"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "melodic-rhythms-vol-4",
