      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "i",
      "granularity_name": "other"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "quarter-note-restraint-for-dialogue",
      "narrative": "Bergonzi prescribes playing solos using only half notes, quarter notes, and dotted quarters to create breathing room and enable rhythmic dialogue with the rhythm section. 'Try playing solos on any of the tunes using only half notes, quarter notes, and dotted quarters... Playing less notes at times allows the music to breath more. It also gives the rhythm section space for a little interaction and dialogue.' Chapter 27, p. 110.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "jerry-bergonzi:melodic-rhythms-vol-4:rhythmic-grammar"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "melodic-rhythms-vol-4",
      "references": [
